---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { emails, site } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'the-service', title: '1. The service' },
  { id: 'early-access', title: '2. Early Access' },
  { id: 'account', title: '3. Account and security' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', title: '4. Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'your-content', title: '5. Your content and platform rules' },
  { id: 'third-party', title: '6. Third-party services' },
  { id: 'open-source', title: '7. Open source' },
  { id: 'disclaimers', title: '8. Disclaimers' },
  { id: 'liability', title: '9. Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'termination', title: '10. Termination' },
  { id: 'law', title: '11. Governing law' },
  { id: 'contact', title: '12. Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using Postmonster: Early Access conditions, account rules, acceptable use, your content and platform rules, open source licensing and liability."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p class="note">
    These terms are a working document for Early Access and are reviewed by the operator.
    They are a starting point, not legal advice to anyone else. Effective date:
    {site.effectiveDate}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-service">1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    Postmonster is a social media scheduling and publishing tool: you connect your own
    channel accounts, create posts, preview them per network, schedule them and track
    their publishing status. The service is operated by {site.legalName} ({site.country}).
    By creating an account you agree to these terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="early-access">2. Early Access</h2>
  <p>
    Postmonster is currently in Early Access. During this period:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The service is provided free of charge; no payment details are required.</li>
    <li>
      Access is invite-only and granted in small batches. We may change, pause or limit
      features while we harden the product.
    </li>
    <li>
      There is no SLA: availability, publishing windows and support response times are
      best effort, though we aim to reply to requests within 3 business days.
    </li>
    <li>
      If pricing is introduced, we will announce it in advance and never charge you
      silently.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="account">3. Account and security</h2>
  <p>
    You must provide accurate information and keep your login credentials confidential.
    You are responsible for the activity in your workspace, including the content your
    team publishes. Tell us promptly at
    <a href={`mailto:${emails.support}`}>{emails.support}</a> if you suspect unauthorized
    access.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to use Postmonster to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>send spam or unsolicited bulk content;</li>
    <li>violate the rules, terms or guidelines of any network you publish to;</li>
    <li>infringe anyone's rights, including copyright, trademark and privacy;</li>
    <li>publish unlawful, deceptive or malicious content;</li>
    <li>probe, disrupt or overload the service or its integrations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may limit or suspend accounts that put the service, its users or the connected
    platforms at risk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-content">5. Your content and platform rules</h2>
  <p>
    You own the content you upload and publish. You grant us only the rights needed to
    store it and deliver it to the networks you choose. You are solely responsible for
    your content and for complying with the rules of each platform — for example the
    <a
      href="https://www.tiktok.com/community-guidelines"
      rel="noopener nofollow"
      target="_blank">TikTok Community Guidelines</a
    > and
    <a
      href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/page/global/bc-policy/en"
      rel="noopener nofollow"
      target="_blank">TikTok Branded Content Policy</a
    >. Commercial content disclosure settings in the tool help you meet platform
    requirements, but the responsibility for correct disclosure is yours.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party">6. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Publishing relies on third-party networks (TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, X and others)
    and their APIs. Their availability, rate limits and policy changes are outside our
    control; a post can fail or be rejected by a platform even when the service works as
    designed. When that happens, we show you the status and the reason we received. Each
    platform's own terms apply to your accounts there.
  </p>

  <h2 id="open-source">7. Open source</h2>
  <p>
    Postmonster is built on the open-source Postiz project and is licensed under the
    GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0). The source code of the deployed
    version is available at <a href={site.sourceCodeUrl}>{site.sourceCodeUrl}</a>. The
    license gives you rights to the code itself; these terms cover the hosted service.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers">8. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided "as is" and "as available". To the extent permitted by law,
    we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including fitness for a particular
    purpose and non-infringement. We do not warrant that publishing will always succeed
    or that the service will be uninterrupted.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, {site.legalName} is not liable for indirect,
    incidental or consequential damages, lost profits, lost data or the consequences of
    content published through the service. Our aggregate liability arising out of these
    terms is limited to the greater of the amounts you paid us in the 12 months before
    the claim or EUR 50. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">10. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the service and delete your account at any time (Settings → delete
    account, with email confirmation). We may suspend or terminate access for material
    breaches of these terms, with notice where reasonably possible. Sections that by
    nature should survive (ownership, disclaimers, liability, governing law) survive
    termination.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {site.country}, without regard to conflict of
    law rules. Mandatory consumer protections of your country of residence remain
    unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${emails.hello}`}>{emails.hello}</a>.
    Support: <a href={`mailto:${emails.support}`}>{emails.support}</a>. Operator:
    {site.legalName}, {site.country}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
